  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_shank_cb1dde1a255eeec32b5f7e21da22b57d489e9dc65c7ca32d281c656ba92e60ca113">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>fur obtained from the legs of animals, especially kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217) | fur obtained from the legs of animals, esp. kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (OED s.v. shank 2) | furs made of the skins from the legs of the animal and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217) | [fox] fur of the leg of the fox | fur obtained from the legs of animals, esp. kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217; OED s.v. shank n. 2) | fur obtained from the legs of animals, especially kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217; OED s.v. shank n. 2) | shanks are fur obtained from the legs of animals, especially kids, goats or sheep, and used for trimming outer garments (Veale 217; OED s.v. shank n. 2), while a tavelyn is a small package of skins or furs, but it is unknown what they designate when used together</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
